Forecasting tourism
ETS forecasts for each series are incoherent.


Code
tourism_purpose &lt;- tourism |&gt; 
  aggregate_key(Purpose, Trips = sum(Trips))
tourism_purpose_fc &lt;- tourism_purpose |&gt; 
  model(ETS(Trips)) |&gt; 
  forecast(h = "2 years")
tourism_purpose_fc |&gt; 
  autoplot(tourism_purpose |&gt; filter(Quarter &gt;= yearquarter("2010 Q1")))

Forecasting tourism
The sum of forecasts for each Purpose (convolution) is not equal to the total.


Code
library(distributional)
tourism_purpose_fc |&gt;
  # Compute the convolution of the base forecasts by Purpose
  filter(!is_aggregated(Purpose)) |&gt;
  group_by(.model) |&gt; 
  summarise(.model = "Sum of base forecasts", Trips = sum(Trips)) |&gt;
  # sum() is invalid somehow? Likely a distributional bug. Recreate it.
  mutate(Trips = dist_normal(mean(Trips), sqrt(variance(Trips)))) |&gt; 
  # Add back the base forecast for total
  bind_rows(
    tourism_purpose_fc |&gt;
      filter(is_aggregated(Purpose)) |&gt;
      transmute(.model = "Forecast of total", Trips)
  ) |&gt;
  # Plot forecasts against the actual total
  autoplot(tourism_purpose |&gt; filter(is_aggregated(Purpose), Quarter &gt;= yearquarter("2010 Q1")) |&gt; select(-Purpose)) +
  facet_grid(vars(.model), scales = "free_y") +
  theme(legend.position = "bottom")

Forecast reconciliation
Now that we have incoherent base forecasts, how can we reconcile them?

data |&gt; 
  aggregate_key(A * B / C, sum(???)) |&gt;
  model(base = ETS(???)) |&gt;
  reconcile(coherent = ???(base)) |&gt;
  forecast()





Single-level methods


Traditionally coherent forecasts were made with only one level of base forecasts from the hierarchy.








All-level methods


Fortunately better methods exist that use information from all base forecasts across the hierarchy.

Forecasting tourism
Estimate base forecasting models.

tourism_agg &lt;- tourism |&gt; 
  aggregate_key(Purpose * (State / Region), Trips = sum(Trips))
tourism_agg |&gt; 
  model(ets = ETS(Trips))

